        "original_id": "3e37d177-f827-5548-807f-1aa6cbd22431",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sandy Fox, Tiggy, Mike Judge, Greg Daniels, Judy and Mary\n- Works: King of the Hill, \"Freckles,\" \"Sobakasu,\" Rurouni Kenshin, \"Why\"\n- Roles: voice actress, singer, dancer\n- Topics: animated cartoons, anime, video games, American animated sitcoms, remix songs\n\nFacts:\n- Sandy Fox was born as Sandra Marie Fox on July 13, 1963.\n- Sandy Fox is an American voice actress, singer, and dancer.\n- Sandy Fox has had numerous roles in animated cartoons, anime, and video games.\n- King of the Hill is an American animated sitcom created by Mike Judge and Greg Daniels.\n- King of the Hill aired on Fox from January 12, 1997 to September 13, 2009.\n- \"Freckles\" is a Sandy Fox song.\n- \"Sobakasu\" is a song by Judy and Mary and was used in the anime Rurouni Kenshin.\n- Tiggy is perhaps best known for her remix of the Sandy Fox song \"Freckles,\" which was originally the English version of \"Sobakasu.\"\n- Tiggy is also popular in parts of Southeast Asia with the song \"Why.\"",
